            <ArticleTitle>Adult peripheral angiography. Results from four North American randomized clinical trials of ionic media vs. iohexol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S108-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four, randomized, double blind comparisons of iohexol versus ionic media for peripheral angiography are summarized. Iohexol is safe, effective, and significantly less painful than ionic media for this indication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
